[38;5;231m⏺[39m I'm treating this as [1mbounded[0m: it changes one existing page and filters in the browser, so I'll give you a short design
  here in chat and won't write a spec. Say so if you'd rather go through the full spec process.

  I need to settle where the controls go before the design, so I've put three wireframes in a browser tab:

  [94m]8;id=1d3lg10;http://localhost:52796/?key=122eef25c1da3a3a8b0ada9dab2af0a40d36cf07560e234148427cee015da854\http://localhost:52796/?key=122eef25c1da3a3a8b0ada9dab2af0a40d36cf07560e234148427cee015da854[39m]8;;\

  - [1mA. Toolbar above the table.[0m An event type dropdown listing all nine types, plus a search box for device or location.
    It's always visible, and a result count sits under it.
  - [1mB. Same as A, plus a "Show failed sign-ins only" button.[0m Your notes say failed sign-ins are what Security wants easy
    to find, and they're what every support ticket so far was about. The active filter shows as a tag you can remove.
  - [1mC. A "Filter" button that opens a popover with the same fields.[0m The page header stays clean, but every filter takes
    an extra click.

  I recommend B. It puts the most common search one click away and adds only one button to A. C hides the controls on a
  page whose whole problem is that people can't find things.

  Have a look and tell me here which you prefer. You can also click an option in the browser.

  The mockups are saved under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the repo root. There's no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet, so that folder should be
  ignored before anything gets committed.

